Explanation of the change:

1. Right before we apply `--fix` or `--quiet`, we call `countErrors(results)` once to stash away the “original” warning count (`originalWarningCount`).
2. We still respect `--quiet` by stripping warnings out of `results` before printing.
3. When evaluating the `--max-warnings` threshold, we compare `originalWarningCount`—the count taken *before* filtering—against `options.maxWarnings`.  This way, even in quiet mode, exceeding the warning limit will produce an exit code of 1 (and emit the “too many warnings” error).
4. All other behavior remains unchanged.
